+### [Differentiable DRR Generation via Vectorized GPU Siddon's Method](9914-differentiable-drr-generation-via-vectorized-gpu-siddon-s-me.md)
+This method generates Digitally Reconstructed Radiographs (DRRs) that are fully differentiable with respect to 7 geometric imaging parameters by reformulating Siddon's ray-tracing algorithm as a series of vectorized tensor operations within PyTorch. It solves the problem of slow gradient-based optimization in intraoperative imaging by leveraging automatic differentiation, avoiding the high memory costs of standard reverse-mode AD and the complexity of adjoint methods. Unlike iterative ray-tracing implementations, it computes all plane intersections in parallel using GPU tensor algebra, trading memory efficiency for speed and compatibility with deep learning frameworks.
 
